# =============================================================================
# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Every Dockerfile here builds from the WORKSPACE ROOT, so without this file the
# context is the entire repo including node_modules, .next and dist — hundreds of
# megabytes shipped to the daemon on every build, and worse, a host-built
# node_modules can shadow the one the image installs. Native binaries compiled
# for Windows do not run on Alpine, so that shadowing fails at runtime rather
# than at build.
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies — the image installs its own with --frozen-lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — the image builds its own.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out

# Nx local cache and daemon state.
.nx

# Secrets. `.env` MUST NOT enter an image: the Dockerfiles take configuration
# through build args and runtime environment, and a baked-in secret survives in
# the layer history even if a later layer deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env*.example

# VCS and tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Tests and fixtures — not needed to build a runtime image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/vitest.setup.ts
**/playwright.config.ts
apps/*-e2e

# Docs and local reference material.
docs
reference
*.md
!README.md

# Local artefacts.
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
